# 8. PERFORMANCE — ABSOLUTELY CRITICAL

A spectacular website that freezes, stutters, or takes forever to load is not acceptable.

Optimize aggressively.

Requirements:

- Lazy-load nonessential scenes.
- Compress textures.
- Use appropriate GLB/GLTF optimization.
- Apply instancing where useful.
- Reduce draw calls.
- Optimize shadow maps.
- Cap device pixel ratio intelligently.
- Reduce postprocessing on weaker devices.
- Avoid unnecessary React rerenders.
- Clean up Three.js resources correctly.
- Manage GPU memory.
- Pause or reduce rendering when appropriate.
- Code-split major features.
- Provide a lightweight loading experience.
- Use CDN caching effectively.
- Avoid unnecessary background network requests.

Target approximately 60 FPS on capable desktop hardware.

On less powerful hardware, prioritize stable interaction and acceptable frame pacing over maximum visual quality.

Measure real performance rather than claiming untested FPS.

Test on integrated graphics as well as stronger desktop hardware when possible.

Provide an explicit performance and quality-mode strategy.

